d by the solver. - **No solver default changes.** Fan order, Theorem 2's switch, the relabelling   portfolio and the rule are measured behind flags that default to today's   behaviour, with paired node counts, and *proposed* in the report. Enabling   any of them is the owner's change. - **Every split groups by file ∪ MOSP-graph isomorphism class**   (`learning.fingerprint.union_groups`; certificates in `learning/data/canonical.csv`   and `learning/data/ensemble/results.csv`). - **Nodes, not seconds**, for every hardness statement; seconds beside them.   A censored call (deadline) is a lower bound, never a missing value. - **State the size range every conclusion covers.** The corpus is 6,376   instances at 9–134 customers; the campaign is 37,800 at 10–40; item 02   extends it to 75 and, on the ridge, 100. Nothing below 100 is evidence about   125×125 except through a stated extrapolation. - Every number in a report is regenerated by a command named in that report. - Findings that rest on a handful of instances are re-certified for those   instances (`solve_mosp_exact`, never `solutions_dir=None`) before being written.  - **Compute**: check `pgrep -f benchmarks.recertify`; if it is running, its   cores are not yours. 32 cores total; use up to 16 here. An RTX 5090 with CUDA   is available. Each iteration has a hard 3-hour wall-clock cap enforced by the   driver; budget so the report section and PROGRESS.md are written well inside   it; the two long-running items (03, 04) price their runs with the ridge law   (§14) before starting them and sample if the full run will not fit, saying so.  ## Current Focus `reports/ml_nature_plan_2.md` §3: fourteen items in dependency order. The differential harness comes first because everything after it rests on the answers being sound.  ## Target Problems (in order) See `iterations.md`. Work on exactly ONE unchecked item per iteration.  ## Acceptance Criteria (per item) - [ ] Code lives under `learning/` (or `lean/` for item 12) with a