s never a bound.** Nothing learned may touch   `satisfiability/mosp_solver.py::_lower_bound` or any path that decides `k`.   A conjectured bound is written up as a conjecture, checked on every certified   instance, attacked by the extremal search, and never used by the solver. - **No solver default changes.** Fan order, Theorem 2's switch, the relabelling   portfolio and the rule are measured behind flags that default to today's   behaviour, with paired node counts, and *proposed* in the report. Enabling   any of them is the owner's change. - **Every split groups by file ∪ MOSP-graph isomorphism class**   (`learning.fingerprint.union_groups`; certificates in `learning/data/canonical.csv`   and `learning/data/ensemble/results.csv`). - **Nodes, not seconds**, for every hardness statement; seconds beside them.   A censored call (deadline) is a lower bound, never a missing value. - **State the size range every conclusion covers.** The corpus is 6,376   instances at 9–134 customers; the campaign is 37,800 at 10–40; item 02   extends it to 75 and, on the ridge, 100. Nothing below 100 is evidence about   125×125 except through a stated extrapolation. - Every number in a report is regenerated by a command named in that report. - Findings that rest on a handful of instances are re-certified for those   instances (`solve_mosp_exact`, never `solutions_dir=None`) before being written.  - **Compute**: check `pgrep -f benchmarks.recertify`; if it is running, its   cores are not yours. 32 cores total; use up to 16 here. An RTX 5090 with CUDA   is available. Each iteration has a hard 3-hour wall-clock cap enforced by the   driver; budget so the report section and PROGRESS.md are written well inside   it; the two long-running items (03, 04) price their runs with the ridge law   (§14) before starting them and sample if the full run will not fit, saying so.  ## Current Focus `reports/ml_nature_plan_2.md` §3: fourteen items in dependency order. The differential harness comes first because everything after it rests on the answers being sound.  ## Target Problems (in order) See `iterations.md`. Work on exactly ONE unchecked item per iteration.  ## Acceptance Criteria (per item) - [ ] Code lives under `learning/` (or `lean/` for item 12) with a module       docstring saying what question it answers and how to run it; runnable as       `python -m learning.<name>`. - [ ] A section appended to `reports/ml_nature.md` (continuing the numbering,       §15 onwards) with: the question, the method, the baseline, the table(s),       the finding in one paragraph, the size range covered, the kill criterion's       verdict where the plan states one, and the regenerate command. - [ ] `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes (~80 s). New code that computes a       quantity gets at least one test on a tiny hand-checkable instance. A new       flag on the search gets a test that the default is unchanged. - [ ] The item is marked `- [x]` (done) or `- [!]` (blocked, with a reason in       PROGRESS.md) in `iterations.md`. - [ ] No regressions, no changes to solver defaults, nothing written to       `solutions/`. Generated instances and witnesses go under       `learning/data/ensemble/` (committed; keep the total under ~120 MB       apparent, and prefer a manifest of seeds to instance files). DRAT proofs       go under `learning/data/proofs/` which item 03 adds to `.gitignore`; only       their hashes, sizes and checker verdicts are committed.  ## Completion Conditions An item is DONE when either: 1. **Solved**: meets all criteria and the report section is written, OR 2. **Blocked**: documented in PROGRESS.md with the specific blocker. Item 12    (Lean) may end blocked with statements and a gap list; that is a deliverable.  ## Context - **Key files**: `learning/ensemble.py` (the campaign: generation, solving,   refuting, features, certificates; resumable), `learning/node_counts.py`   (`refute`, `refutation_kwargs`: the per-call primitive and the two   configurations), `learning/degeneracy.py` (the lattice oracle,   `optimal_choices`, `count_search`), `learning/graph_story.py` (relabelling   and re-covering primitives from §13), `learning/scale_test.py`   (`fit_scaling`, the corpus node counts in `learning/data/ensemble/scale_nodes.csv`),   `learning/hardness_map.py`, `learning/concentration.py`,   `learning/formula_search.py` (the enumerator for conjecture mining),   `learning/bound_gap.py` (`treewidth_upper_bound`, `describe_instance`, the   ten smallest gap instances), `learning/distil.py` (the two-key rule and the   lexicographic family), `satisfiability/customer_search.py` (`decide`,   `sparse_enough_for_better_move`, the C path), `satisfiability/heuristics.py`   (`restricted_dfs`), `satisfiability/mosp_encoding.py` and `mosp_solver.py`   (the SAT path; pysat `Solver(name='cadical195', with_proof=True)` works on   this machine, drat-trim does not exist yet and must be built),   `lean/MOSPFormalization/` (`Pathwidth.lean`, `VertexSeparation.lean`,   `VSEquivPW.lean`, `ForMathlib/`), `recertify/results.json` (the 125×125   counts and what recertify spent). - **Data**: `solutions/*.json` (read-only here); `learning/data/ensemble/`   (37,800 campaign rows, witnesses, `scale_nodes.csv`, `recover*.csv`,   `relabel.csv.gz`); `learning/data/canonical.csv`, `instances.csv`,   `node_counts.csv`, `degeneracy.csv`. - **Testing**: `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x`. - **Dependencies**: `learning/requirements.txt`; new packages only behind soft   imports (lifelines or scikit-survival for item 05; drat-trim is a C binary,   build it under `tools/` from its public source if network access allows,   else record the blocker).  ## Important Notes - Do NOT run `benchmarks.csearch`, `benchmarks.recertify`, `benchmarks.overnight`   or any sweep that writes to `solutions/`. Generated instances are solved with   `solve_mosp_exact(..., solutions_dir=<learning/data/ensemble/solutions>)`. - Do NOT edit `CLAUDE.md`; the loop's owner folds findings in afterwards. - Do NOT rewrite existing report sections; append. If a finding contradicts an   earlier one, say so in the new section and leave the old one in place. - Commit nothing yourself; the driver commits after tests pass. - You are running in print mode: **ending your turn ends the session.** Never   end a turn waiting on a background job. Run studies in the foreground or poll   them in a bounded loop, and do not stop until the report section,   PROGRESS.md and iterations.md are written. - When stopping a background process, match its PID or an anchored pattern,   never a bare `pkill -f <word>`. - Method notes inherited (`CLAUDE.md`): build feature sets from   `learning.features.feature_names` group names, never from every numeric   column; never `fork` a pool after LightGBM has run (`spawn` with an   initializer); PySR at 4 threads and 2,000 iterations; round `aut_order`   before integer division; plot density as realised `col_mean`, not nominal   `p`; the recertify configuration equals `csearch` on instances with ≤ 5   products per customer; a column-key collision once overwrote a table column   silently, so key tables by full names.   --- PROGRESS.md (most recent iterations at the bottom) --- # Progress Log  ## Ralph Loop 0003 Status - **Started**: 2026-09-26 10:23 - **Target**: 14 items - **Current**: 4/14 SOLVED  ---  ## Iteration 1 — 2026-09-26 10:48  **Item 01 · §2.1(a) The differential harness** — SOLVED, with a finding the plan expected not to make.  ### Completed - `learning/differential.py`: for every certified instance, the identity, 8   seeded relabellings and one re-covering (`graph_story` primitives), each   decided at `optimum − 1` and `optimum` under both `node_counts`   configurations, the `sat` side's closing order simulated; disagreements,   contradictions and lattice-oracle mismatches kept apart; every node count   recorded. Stages: `run`, `tables`, `drawn` (re-certifies flagged instances   by routes independent of the C `better_move` and classifies which rule   pairing each false answer needs). - The run: 43,935 instances (campaign 37,800 at 10–40; corpus 6,135 at 9–40),   878,700 runs, 1,757,280 decision calls, 199 s on 16 workers. Zero   disagreements at `optimum − 1` (878,580 of 878,580 `unsat`), zero `unknown`,   zero witness failures, zero oracle mismatches on 13,612 instances. - **56 disagreements at `k = optimum`** (46 campaign, 10 corpus), 88 false   `unsat` answers, all under the `csearch` configuration (Theorem 2 on). All   56 stored optima re-certified independently (Python reference, C default,   cached solve, lattice oracle on 11): the values are right, the rule is   wrong. Mechanism: the C `better_move` composed with `subset_rule` (78 of   88) or `definite_move` (3 of 88) forms a cross-rule dominance cycle;   `better_move` alone is sound on all 88. Traced at the root of   `ens_f_n10_m20_d2_i070`; flag sweeps on two instances; minimal 10×13 and   17×9 sub-instances. Fix proposed in §15, **not applied**. - Relabelling spread by size band and configuration, refutation and witness   sides (item 04's input): at n ≤ 40 min-of-9 beats the identity by ≥ 1.5× on   under 0.1% of instances under `default` for refutations, 16–17% for witness   searches at 36–40. - Re-covering invariants of §13 confirmed on all 43,935: default node counts   equal on every pair at both k; csearch differences only inside   `better_move` flips. - `reports/ml_nature.md` §15; `reports/differential_tables.md`;   `learning/data/ensemble/differential.csv.gz` (5.5 MB), `differential_summary.csv`,   `differential_drawn.csv`, `differential_drawn_rules.csv` (11 MB total). - `tests/test_differential.py`: 11 tests pass, including the planted liar   (one relabelling lies at the optimum; the harness names it) and a liar at   `optimum − 1`; one strict `xfail` pins the C failure on the drawn instance   and will XPASS-fail when the C is fixed. Full suite: 824 passed, 2 skipped,   2 xfailed in 79 s.  ### Blockers - None for the item. **Alert 